# Never ship local secrets or scratch state into a deployment bundle.
#
# The Vercel CLI uploads the working directory, and without this file the local
# .env - which holds live Stripe, R2 and Google credentials - is packaged and
# read during the build. Verified: before this existed, the build logged
# "Environment variables loaded from .env" and picked up the local SQLite URL.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.scratch
.vercel
prisma/dev.db
*.db
*.db-journal
prisma/schema.postgres.prisma
.next
node_modules
shots
scripts/.frames
*.log
